 "text": "Hey there, how are you? How many miles you put on each year? For most riders, it's once a month or when the tyres feel worn. The tyre's tyre pressure rating is usually printed on sidewall. It' bit lower than you want when you feel the tyre. If you don't know, a common rule is one fifth of your bike's weight in pounds, plus a bit extra. Yes, a little. Lower pressure letting the tyre float on the road gives better grip, but only little, and only on smooth roads.",
